    "created_at": "2017-06-15T13:43:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-15T13:43:44Z",
    "body": "I don't understand the question. The httpRequest object is a copy of the request, including all of its headers. When a redirect is processed later (in step 5 of https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-http-fetch) we use the original request object, not the copy that was used in http-network-or-cache-fetch.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
